   "translation": {
    "literal": "To the eastern quarter salutation. To the southern quarter salutation. To the western quarter salutation. To the northern quarter salutation. To the above salutation. To the below salutation. To the mid-region salutation. To the Earth salutation. To Brahmā salutation. To Viṣṇu salutation. To Death salutation.",
    "readable": "Salutation to the east, the south, the west and the north; to what is above and what is below; to the sky and to the Earth; to Brahmā, to Viṣṇu, and to Death."
   }
  }
 ],
 "meaning": "The worshipper turns and bows to each of the four quarters, then upwards and downwards, to the sky and the earth, and to the deities Brahmā and Viṣṇu, ending with Death (Mṛtyu), which leads into the salutation to Yama that follows. The stotrasamhita text marks each with its direction (above for the sky and Brahmā, below for the earth and Viṣṇu). M’s list repeats the quarters and ends differently (corrections.json).",
 "in_the_rite": "Step dig-vandana, after the abhivādana, in all three services.",
 "notes": [
  {
   "label": "direct",
   "text": "Each line is a name in the dative with namaḥ; the four quarters are feminine adjectives agreeing with diś, ‘direction’."
  }
 ],
